<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="007" project="spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>Playbook run authorization into one shared method</title>
    <phase>0 Removal, prerequisites and seams</phase>
    <gate>after 001 (same filter file)</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Tags include bff-api and auth; refactors PlaybookAuthorizationFilter (.cs) with frozen REST responses</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Authorization refactor on a security filter (playbook access, document access, subject checks, parameter policy) whose REST behaviour must stay identical</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>B</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Edits only PlaybookAuthorizationFilter.cs (after 001 has finished with it) and new playbook-auth tests; no other Wave 2 task touches them</parallel-reason>
    <deps>001</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, auth, refactoring, integration-test</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-5 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Move the Run-mode checks of PlaybookAuthorizationFilter (playbook use, document access, subject checks, parameter policy) into one public method that takes the request HttpContext and the run inputs and returns a typed authorization result; the filter calls it and maps the result to exactly today's responses, so task 030's spaarke_run_playbook can call the same method instead of copying checks.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Expert in ASP.NET Core endpoint filters and caller-scoped authorization.</role>
  <goal>A single method (for example PlaybookRunAuthorization.AuthorizeRunAsync) owns the run checks; PlaybookAuthorizationFilter's Run mode is a thin caller; POST /api/ai/playbooks/{id}/execute returns byte-identical 400/403/404/202 responses; the typed result carries a reasonCode an MCP tool can return.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-05 prerequisite and MUST NOT ("move authorization checks to one shared method that REST and MCP both call"). After task 001, AuthorizeRunAsync (PlaybookAuthorizationFilter.cs ~:560) handles only ExecutePlaybookRequest. Existing public statics to reuse: BuildPlaybookUseCheckAsync (:307, :339), UniformPlaybookNotFound (:368), UniformRecordAccessDenied (:382), ResolveCallerSystemUserIdAsync (:394), GetRunUserId (:650), ParameterRejected (:664), BuildSubjectRunChecksAsync (:715), IsPlaybookUseAllowedForCallerAsync (:801). Line numbers shift after 001; re-read the file.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Filters/PlaybookAuthorizationFilter.cs</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/auth/Ai/PlaybookRunAuthorizationSharedMethodTests.cs</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/integration/contract/Api/Ai/PlaybookRouteAuthorizationContractTests.cs (execute-route contract; must pass unchanged)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Signals/DecisionResultMapper.cs (one typed result mapped to REST and MCP)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PlaybookParameterPolicy.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="001" status="pending">Agent branch removed from the same filter</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-008">The shared method is the only implementation of the Run-mode checks; PlaybookAuthorizationFilter's Run mode binds the request, calls it, and maps its result; no check is duplicated. Other modes (Owner, Access, ById, TablePrivilege, PublicFlagShare) are not changed.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">REST responses of POST /api/ai/playbooks/{id}/execute stay byte-for-byte unchanged (status, ProblemDetails type/title/detail/extensions) for every case PlaybookRouteAuthorizationContractTests covers; the Dataverse access-call sequence and count are unchanged.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-019">The typed result carries a stable reasonCode per refusal (the same codes the REST ProblemDetails expose, or new codes recorded in the task notes if REST exposes none) so task 030 can return it through McpToolResults; it carries no ProblemDetails or IResult.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">The method takes the request HttpContext and fails closed (UserContextRequired) when it is null or unauthenticated; no app-only fallback.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-013">The method lives in Api/Filters/ (or Services/Ai/PublicContracts/ if MCP tools must reach it without referencing filter internals; record the choice) and exposes no AI-internal type in its signature.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-029">Every change this task makes under src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ is listed in the PR with a Placement Justification that cites .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md (source: spec.md 'Placement &amp; New Components'), and the PR records the publish-size delta against a fresh master build per .claude/constraints/azure-deployment.md 'BFF Publish-Size Per-Task Verification Rule': +5 MB or more needs explicit justification, 55 MB total triggers architecture review, 60 MB is a hard stop. No new HIGH CVE (dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">Every test this task adds lives on a KEEP path (tests/integration/{auth,contract,regression,data-mutation}/** or tests/unit/domain/**), mocks only at module boundaries, and uses no Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt; or Mock&lt;IServiceClient&gt;.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Before each push run bash scripts/quality/check-changed-cs-format.sh origin/master and /conflict-check. CS0618 is a build error: migrate, never suppress.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/api.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/api/endpoint-definition.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/api/endpoint-filters.md</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/auth.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/auth/spaarke-sso-binding.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/auth/obo-flow.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/auth/oauth-scopes.md</file>
      <file>docs/guides/auth-deployment-setup.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/testing.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/testing/unit-test-structure.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/testing/mocking-patterns.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-008-endpoint-filters.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-013-ai-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-019-problemdetails.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-028-spaarke-auth-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-029-bff-publish-hygiene.md</file>
      <file>docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r2/spec.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r2/CLAUDE.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Run PlaybookRouteAuthorizationContractTests green on the post-001 code and note the execute-route cases.</step>
    <step order="2">Extract the Run-mode body into the shared method with a typed result; make the filter call it and map results to the existing responses.</step>
    <step order="3">Write PlaybookRunAuthorizationSharedMethodTests for the criteria (calling the method directly, as task 030 will).</step>
    <step order="4">Run the playbook contract and auth suites; measure the publish-size delta.</step>
    <step order="5">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` (the bracketed ASCII token is mandatory, the emoji alone is not greppable: task-create Step 5, FAILURE-MODES G-16), set the POML &lt;status&gt; to completed, and run pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1</step>
    <step order="6">If any deviations from plan, document in projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r2/notes/ (decisions go to notes/decisions.md)</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If keeping the REST responses identical requires the filter to keep any check of its own beyond binding and mapping, STOP and escalate: the shared method must be the single owner.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>notes/reuse-scan.md row "Playbook run start and status": Api/Filters/PlaybookAuthorizationFilter.cs:127 "the filter's checks move into a shared method". CAPABILITY-INDEX: no playbook-auth row (grep "PlaybookAuthorization" .claude/patterns/CAPABILITY-INDEX.md).</existing>
    <extension>Yes, extended in place: the filter's own logic becomes a callable method in the same file; no new class unless placement requires PublicContracts.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Task 030's run tool would have to copy the playbook, document, subject and parameter checks (spec MUST NOT), giving the rule two owners that can drift.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/, dotnet test, dotnet publish</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Filters/PlaybookAuthorizationFilter.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/auth/Ai/PlaybookRunAuthorizationSharedMethodTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">PlaybookRouteAuthorizationContractTests passes unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Calling the shared method directly for an allowed caller, playbook and document returns Allowed.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a playbook the caller may not use returns the uniform-not-found result with its reasonCode; a document the caller cannot read returns the record-access-denied result; a rejected parameter returns the parameter-rejected result; each matches the REST status for the same input.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a null HttpContext or unauthenticated principal returns UserContextRequired and makes no Dataverse call.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">grep shows the Run-mode checks implemented once (the filter contains no playbook-use, document-access or subject check of its own in Run mode).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The PR records the publish-size delta (total at or under 60 MB), no new HIGH CVE, and the uac-r2 and ontology-r1 reviews.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named in these criteria; anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-05 prerequisite. Two adversarial-verifier passes (auth).</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Before starting, load all files listed in &lt;knowledge&gt;&lt;files&gt;. Follow task-execute for the pre-execution checklist.</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
